WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.160
By now you may have noticed how physically demanding and exhausting performing CPR can

00:00:06.160 --> 00:00:07.240
be.

00:00:07.240 --> 00:00:11.440
Because the quality of your chest compressions will naturally start to decrease as you get

00:00:11.440 --> 00:00:15.920
tired, it is vital to use the people around you for support.

00:00:15.920 --> 00:00:22.000
Whenever possible, you should alternate performing CPR with another person every two minutes,

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:25.559
which is about five rounds of the 30 to 2 ratio.

00:00:25.559 --> 00:00:30.760
This rotation keeps the compressions effective and prevents total exhaustion.

00:00:30.760 --> 00:00:33.200
Don't hesitate to take charge of the scene.

00:00:33.200 --> 00:00:39.060
Remember to avoid generic shouts like someone call 911 because it can lead to bystander

00:00:39.060 --> 00:00:41.520
effect where no one takes action.

00:00:41.520 --> 00:00:47.040
Instead, point to a specific person and assign them a clear role, such as calling emergency

00:00:47.040 --> 00:00:50.720
services or directing the ambulance when it arrives.

00:00:50.720 --> 00:00:56.119
Staying calm and in control allows you to manage the situation effectively until professional

00:00:56.119 --> 00:00:57.480
help can take over.

